/-!
Adapted from the checked Chapter15 MarkedMS.G2Reconstruction proof to the
exceptional MS2(b) input. Only the two-group and core-containment consequences
of MS2 are used; the original SmallMSPair interface is unchanged.

# The actual G₂ radius group and its terminal size obstruction

The original MS product generates every vertex stabilizer by its two-residual
and the incident edge kernel. It follows that the radius group V is generated
by its moving subgroup Vcirc and the edge radius, which is elementary abelian.
Consequently [V,V] = [Vcirc,V], and the involutory radius generators give
Φ(V) = [V,V]. These equalities retain the actual ambient subgroup inclusions.

At a critical midpoint, the commutator of the two endpoint seeds maps onto
the fixed three-space of the natural G₂ offender. Thus [Vcirc,V] has at least
eight elements. This contradicts the order-two bound in the fixed-derived
branch on printed p.879, when that bound is supplied. The fixed-derived
reduction and its module calculation are not asserted by this module.

The radius-generation argument adapts the earlier binary `Exclusion.Radius`
proof, replacing its residual-plus-core generation by residual-plus-edge
generation, which also handles the full G₂(2) outer action. The deliberate
`import all` reuses its internal join-normalization lemma; no private name
occurs in the public statements.
Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher, *Pushing up weak BN-pairs of rank two*,
(3.8), printed pp.878--879; Aschbacher--Smith C.1.31--32, pp.135--136.
-/

